{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'","aggregated_output":"# Working in this repository\n\nAxylo is a browser charting library. The product is specified in `docs/02-product-spec.md`; the build plan is `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md`. Read the sections your task names before writing code.\n\n## Rules for every change\n\n- **Contracts are fixed.** `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` and `packages/axylo/src/public.ts` are the interfaces between modules. Do not edit them. If your work needs a change there, stop that part, finish what you can, and describe the exact change you need in your report.\n- **Stay in your files.** Each task lists the directories it owns. Do not create, edit or delete anything else, including configuration and other modules. Several agents work in this checkout at the same time.\n- **No runtime dependencies.** Use the platform (`Intl`, typed arrays). Dev dependencies already installed: TypeScript, Vitest, fast-check, esbuild, Playwright (system Chrome), axe-core. The network is not available; do not try to install anything.\n- **No DOM at import time.** A module that needs the DOM takes it as a parameter or touches it inside a function. Pure stages (data, scales, formatting, layout, scene) must run in Node.\n- **Hot paths use typed arrays.** No object per data point, no array of arrays per data point, no copying of large columns that the contracts say are borrowed.\n- **Never guess silently.** Anything that cannot be drawn as given is reported through the `DiagnosticSink` with the code from spec section 3.5.\n- **Tests come from the spec.** Expected values are derived from the specification and the fixture data, never by running the implementation and pasting its output. Use fast-check property tests for invariants (\"for any data …\"). A test you cannot make pass is reported as failing; do not weaken it or change its expected value.\n- **TypeScript strict, no `any`** in exported signatures. `__DEV__` is a build-time boolean (true in tests).\n- **Comments say why**, not what. Names are plain words.\n- **Do not commit.** The coordinator commits.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck      # tsc over the library, its tests, and the API examples in docs/api\nnpm test               # unit and property tests (Node)\nnpm run build          # packages/axylo/dist\nnpm run test:browser   # browser tests against the built bundle, in system Chrome\n```\n\n## Your report\n\nEnd with a short report: what you built (files), what you verified and how (paste the last lines of the test run), what is not done or not verified, any contract change you need, and any place where the spec was ambiguous and what you assumed. Keep \"ran and saw\" apart from \"expect\".\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core1.review.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core1.review.md'","aggregated_output":"**Five findings block release.** A strict rejection can alter later data, an encoding update can resurrect evicted rows, and two paths let the reader interact with data that differs from the displayed chart.\n\n**Ran** means I reproduced the result in Node. For controller experiments I used the repository’s controller, data, view, layout, scene, lookup, and reader code, with a manual animation-frame queue and recording substitutes for the browser outputs. **Reasoned** identifies conclusions from source inspection. I did not launch a browser.\n\n### Blocking\n\n1. **B · A rejected strict append mutates the accepted store. Ran.** I created eight series under `strict`, then appended a ninth. The call threw `AX130` and the displayed frame still had eight series. A subsequent valid append to an existing series also threw `AX130`. After disabling strict mode, the rejected ninth series appeared. `store.append()` commits before `finish()` validates the new view. Plan 1.5 requires rejection to preserve the store as well as the visible frame. Prepare the append and its view in a transaction, then commit both after validation. The existing strict-append test exercises an early `NaN` rejection only. [chart.ts:350](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:350) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:229](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:229)\n\n2. **B · Re-encoding an aligned chart loses appended data and restores evicted data. Ran.** Starting at x values `[1,2,3]`, I appended `4` with `keep:2`. The chart showed `[3,4]`. Changing `y` to another valid field restored `[1,2,3]`. A chart created empty, populated by append, then re-encoded became empty again. Explicitly updating `data` with the original array after an append also failed to replace the stream. The controller keeps the initial `options.data` alongside the live store and detects replacement by identity. Plan 1.5 requires call order to determine the data. Re-encode from the retained logical table, honor an explicit data replacement after streaming, and advance the frame epoch on encoding changes as the frame contract requires. [chart.ts:308](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:308) · [contracts.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:129)\n\n3. **B · Eviction changes hover events before the new frame is drawn. Ran.** With `[0,1,2]` displayed, I appended `3` with `keep:1` and moved the simulated pointer over `0` before running the frame. The event contained `x:0, y:0, index:0, row:null` for a real input row. The old lookup still supplies the displayed values, but its row source reads the already-trimmed store. Plan 1.5 and DX5 require all parts of that event to come from the displayed revision. Retain evicted source rows until the last displayed frame that can address them is retired. [chart.ts:794](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:794) · [store-rows.ts:107](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts:107)\n\n4. **B · A deferred failure leaves an active old lookup and can permanently clear axis text. Ran.** I forced the reader stage to fail after a successful draw. The controller emitted the internal-error figure and cleared the text. Moving the pointer then produced the old tooltip. After removing the failure and issuing a title update, the controller resumed drawing with zero axis labels because the cached layout still compared equal. `failSafe()` retains the old ready display, lookup, and layout after clearing their outputs. Publish a complete error-state revision with interaction disabled, invalidate the cleared outputs, and settle readiness against that revision. The browser failure test ends before either hover or recovery. [chart.ts:699](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:699) · [chart.ts:663](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:663) · [data.browser.test.ts:121](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts:121)\n\n5. **B · The full figure has no keyboard, legend, streaming, or table controls. Reasoned from the DOM construction. Ran the zoom subscription.** The figure mounts its caption, plot, note, live region, and tooltip. Nothing mounts a focusable plot, toolbar, legend toggles, Pause/Resume, or the reader’s table. A note can say “See table” with no way to open one, and L8’s small-chart fallback lacks its table control. The controller accepts `select` and `zoom` listeners but only emits `hover`. My programmatic zoom produced zero zoom events. Wire the full-chart controls, visibility state, table model, and events to the displayed revision as specified in plan 1.4, 1.5 and 2.4. Preserve the compact chart’s static behavior. [figure.ts:105](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:105) · [chart.ts:183](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:183) · [chart.ts:797](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:797)\n\n### Major\n\n6. **M · Callbacks can repeat delivery or continue work after destruction. Ran.** An `onDiagnostic` handler that updated only `description` received the same diagnostic twice. A handler that destroyed the chart on its first diagnostic still received the next one. Likewise, a second hover listener ran after the first destroyed the chart. Destroying from a formatter during a frame allowed that frame to draw and repopulate `drawn`. Commit the delivery snapshot before invoking author code, and check the lifecycle generation after callbacks and before publishing frame work. DX5 teardown must take effect inside callbacks too. [chart.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:285) · [chart.ts:677](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:677) · [chart.ts:800](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:800)\n\n7. **M · Scatter and donut append change the meaning of existing data. Ran.** On scatter with x values `[10,20]`, appending `5` with `keep:2` retained `[5,20]` and produced no `AX151`. Plan 1.5 requires the out-of-order diagnostic and the latest two distinct x positions, `[10,20]`. On both scatter and donut, appending one clean row to typed columns changed an existing silent `NaN` into `AX103`. `appendRows()` materializes every old column row and trims by raw arrival order, also renumbering retained rows. Preserve column missingness and source indexes, normalize ordering keys before eviction, and validate the incoming batch before trimming. For donut, I treated the label as its retention key, as the implementation does. [chart.ts:354](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:354) · [chart.ts:1006](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:1006)\n\n8. **M · The empty-state test disagrees with the visible geometry and suppresses omission notes. Ran.** A line joining `(0,0)` and `(10,10)`, zoomed to `[2,4]`, produced “No data to show” and zero marks despite its segment crossing the entire window. Scatter with the same x positions and zoom produced axes, no state message, and a reader summary saying there was no data. An all-invalid compact chart also suppressed its omission marker. The aligned check counts only sample centers, the scatter check counts points anywhere in the series, and the figure drops the note whenever the display is non-ready. Derive drawable content from the view’s draw ranges and visible points. Preserve F12/C5 disclosures when every value is omitted. [chart.ts:941](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:941) · [chart.ts:597](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:597)\n\n9. **M · Live-edge following survives a domain change that moves the window away from the edge. Ran.** I zoomed `[0,5,10]` to `[5,10]`, then replaced the data with a range ending at `15`. The displayed window remained `[5,10]`. Appending `20` jumped it to `[15,20]`. Plan 1.5 says a window away from the latest edge stays put. Reconcile the effective zoom and follow flag together whenever data or author bounds change. The existing follow test uses consecutive appends without an intervening domain update. [chart.ts:316](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:316) · [chart.ts:395](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:395)\n\n10. **M · Synchronous validation gives different answers depending on the entry point. Ran.** For a bar with `y.domain:[1,3]`, `validate()` returned `[]`, creation reported `AX110`, and a clean append removed `AX110` while the domain still excluded zero. Separately, a strict numeric chart threw `AX107` from `zoom(['oops','bad'])`, although spec 3.5 limits strict throws to create, update, and append. A rejected strict append also skipped console and listener delivery entirely. Share the DOM-free validation stages, retain the complete set of applicable findings separately from newly delivered findings, and make strict rejection specific to the public operation. Publish rejected-call diagnostics without replacing `chart.diagnostics`. [index.ts:41](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:41) · [chart.ts:220](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:220) · [chart.ts:264](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:264)\n\n11. **M · Presentation diagnostics arrive late and outlive their cause. Ran.** A throwing tick formatter produced `AX160` with no reader note on the failing frame. Replacing it with a working formatter left `AX160` in `chart.diagnostics` and then displayed the stale warning note. A formatter that threw only for a hovered interior value added `AX160` to the getter without invoking `onDiagnostic` at discovery. The presentation map only inserts a code/field once, while disclosure is computed before formatting completes. Track findings by producing stage and revision, retire them when inputs change, and deliver pointer-origin findings immediately. [chart.ts:454](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:454) · [chart.ts:575](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:575) · [chart.ts:751](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:751)\n\n12. **M · Teardown leaves ownership behind in three lifecycle paths. Reasoned.** A retained destroyed handle still closes over `accepted`, the options store, source data, and DOM references. Removing a target without `destroy()` leaves document, media-query, and font listeners retaining the chart. A setup exception after the figure is appended but before the `try` around `update(input)` bypasses cleanup. Even ordinary teardown after drawing leaves chart-written `--axylo-backdrop` and series properties on the target. Use a disposable controller state, register cleanup as each setup step succeeds, restore owned styles, and release subscriptions on permanent detachment. The heap tests discard every handle. The pointer teardown test dispatches on the root, although the listener was attached to its child plot. [chart.ts:408](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:408) · [chart.ts:854](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:854) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285)\n\n13. **M · A short, visible container can alternate between showing and hiding its fallback. Ran the controller transitions. Reasoned about CSS feedback.** Feeding plot heights `30,0,30,0` yielded summary visibility `true,false,true,false`. In a definite-height flex figure, showing the summary can consume the last 30 pixels, which hides the summary and gives those pixels back. Deferring the ResizeObserver callback moves this cycle across frames. Also, after a caption changes height, `size ??= measure()` can draw once at the previous size. Distinguish an externally hidden container from a visible figure whose caption consumed its plot space, and base L8 fallback on a stable available size. [chart.ts:602](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:602) · [chart.ts:612](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:612) · [css.ts:113](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:113)\n\n14. **M · Font loading invalidates layout but preserves fallback-font widths. Ran the measurer. Reasoned about browser typography.** A measuring context first returned `7` for a label, then `17` after a simulated font load. Even a new measurer for the same document returned the cached `7`. The width cache omits `fontEpoch`, and its 4,096-entry limit applies separately to an unbounded number of styles. A resize also leaves `textStyleDirty` untouched, so responsive CSS can change font or spacing without updating metrics. Invalidate measured widths on font load, bound the whole document cache, and reread computed typography on relevant size changes. Apply supported letter and word spacing to the measuring context as plan 2.2 specifies. [environment.ts:77](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/environment.ts:77) · [chart.ts:811](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:811) · [chart.ts:837](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:837)\n\n15. **M · Continuous bars get a second domain expansion that the layout cache cannot identify. Ran.** With an explicit x domain `[0,20]`, the chart emitted ticks from `-5` to `25`. With fixed bounds `[0,100]`, replacing two x positions `[10,20]` with `[10,90]` produced equal layout keys even though the requested projection changed from `[-5,105]` to `[-40,140]`. `barDomain()` adds spacing after the view has already selected the effective bounds. Use the view’s domain consistently for ticks, marks, and lookup. If layout needs a distinct projection, key its actual bounds. [axes.ts:76](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:76) · [axes.ts:123](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:123) · [axes.ts:143](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:143)\n\n16. **M · Donut color pins can paint the wrong slice. Ran the scene and theme inputs.** For `Empty:0, Sales:4` with a color pinned to `Sales`, the controller supplied palette keys `[\"Empty\",\"Sales\"]`. The sole visible arc requested palette index `0`, the `Empty` slot. This breaks DX6 precisely when two charts have different subsets of drawable slices. Build the theme binding array from each slice’s assigned `colorIndex` and author label. Test a zero-valued slice before a pinned positive slice. [chart.ts:469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:469) · [view/donut.ts:61](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/donut.ts:61)\n\n17. **M · Static aligned charts eagerly copy borrowable columns, and domain-only updates pay that cost again. Ran.** For ascending `Float64Array` x and y columns, neither resulting frame buffer shared the caller’s buffer. All line, area, and bar creates go through the mutable streaming store. A change to `x.domain` alone then incremented the normalize counter. Plan 1.2 specifies borrowed typed columns, and 2.2 assigns author domains to the view stage. Preserve the borrowed frame until a write requires owned storage, and distinguish changes to parsing or fields from changes to presentation or bounds. [chart.ts:244](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:244) · [chart.ts:318](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:318) · [store-buffers.ts:26](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:26)\n\n18. **M · Caption-only updates rebuild lookup, including the scatter spatial index. Ran the stage counters.** Updating only `description` reran `lookup`. Every `finish()` creates a fresh messages object, and lookup and reader both key on its identity. Separately, changing an aligned line’s interior sample count reran layout with the same endpoint ranges and tick inputs because the key includes slot indexes. Reuse resolved messages while overrides are unchanged, and include slot-dependent geometry only for chart types that consume it. The title-only test explicitly checks five unaffected stages and omits lookup. [chart.ts:273](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:273) · [chart.ts:649](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:649) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:173](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:173)\n\n19. **M · Figure naming and state text have inaccessible combinations. Reasoned from the figure. Ran the compact state model.** `labelledBy:'missing'` suppresses AX140 and installs a dangling ID reference without a fallback name. Providing both a valid `labelledBy` and a title still creates an internal heading, contrary to plan 2.4’s external-heading case. Generated IDs can also collide with an existing page ID such as `axylo-1-t`. On a compact loading chart with data, I observed the ordinary data summary as its description while “Loading chart” was only a descendant of `role=\"img\"`. Resolve the naming target, allocate collision-free IDs, and include the current state in the compact image’s accessible description. Test these combinations in the accessibility tree. [chart.ts:146](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:146) · [chart.ts:233](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:233) · [figure.ts:122](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:122)\n\n### Minor\n\n20. **m · The `validate()` type overload accepts options belonging to a different chart. Reasoned.** The first overload pairs any of `'line' | 'area' | 'bar'` with the union of all three option types. An area-only `stacked` or bar-only `layout` option can therefore type-check for `validate('line', …)` and then produce `AX150` at runtime. Give each discriminant its matching options overload. Add the negative example against the package entry point. The existing API examples import the separate declaration sketch. [index.ts:35](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:35) · [examples.ts:2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/api/examples.ts:2)\n\n### Verification\n\nNo files changed. No change to `contracts.ts` or `public.ts` is needed. `npm run typecheck` passed on the final run. I ran the three scoped core test files with Vitest’s filesystem caches disabled. The last lines were:\n\n```text\n Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  20 passed (20)\n   Start at  03:20:10\n   Duration  438ms (transform 68%, tests 16%, import 14%, worker 2%)\n```\n\nBrowser pixels, actual announcements, accessibility trees, heap behavior, and CSP enforcement remain unverified in this review. The scoped chart tests also lack end-to-end checks for continuous resize at the fallback boundary, late font metrics, compact 24×16 sizing, navigation through an intervening failed frame, and the reduced-motion first-frame comparison.\n\n### Areas examined and found sound\n\n- **Ordinary call order and coalescing.** Ran replacement → append → zoom and observed one draw with the requested window. Append → fresh data replacement discarded the append.\n- **Nested patch semantics.** Ran whole-object `title` and `x` replacements. Omitted nested properties reverted to defaults. The scoped property test also passed for absent and explicitly `undefined` keys.\n- **Ordinary explicit destruction.** Ran destroy before the first frame, repeated destroy, and subsequent update, append, and zoom. No later frame or stage ran.\n- **Console deduplication for accepted diagnostics.** The tests passed for one print per code per document and development-only hint printing. The weak document key and finite registry bound this cache.\n- **Environment resolution and DPR.** Ran locale override and document-language fallback. A simulated DPR change reran scene and draw while preserving normalization and layout.\n- **Text insertion and motion.** Source inspection found text-node insertion for author strings and formatter output, visually hidden summary text connected by `aria-describedby`, and no animation in the reviewed rendering path.\n- **Public loading and benchmark gating.** Both existing distribution bundles imported without a DOM and returned `AX103` for the invalid fixture. A production-mode controller exposed `__bench` only with the flag enabled. The renderer switch is absent from the public chart option types.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
