arts[1] + '-' + (parts[2] ?? '01') + '-' + (parts[3] ?? '01') + 'T00:00:00Z');\n    }\n    if (kind === 'wall' || kind === 'time') {\n      const position = instant(raw, kind);\n      if (kind === 'wall' && Number.isFinite(position)) reports.add('AX112', 'none', row);\n      return position;\n    }\n    return NaN;\n  }\n\n  read(raw: unknown, row: number, reports: Reports, omitted = 1): number {\n    if (raw === undefined) {\n      reports.add('AX102', 'omitted', row, undefined, undefined, { amount: omitted, outcome: 'The affected row is not drawn.' });\n      return NaN;\n    }\n    const result = this.parse(raw, row, reports);\n    if (!Number.isFinite(result)) {\n      const fix = this.scatter && this.kind === 'category'\n        ? 'Use a numeric, calendar date or time field for scatter x values.'\n        : undefined;\n      reports.add('AX107', 'omitted', row, raw, fix, { amount: omitted });\n    }\n    return result;\n  }\n\n  restore(categoryCount: number, dateUnit: DateUnit | null): void {\n    this.dateUnit = dateUnit;\n    if (!this.names) return;\n    while (this.categoryCount > categoryCount) this.indexes!.delete(this.names.pop()!);\n  }\n\n  column(values: Float64Array, snapshotCategories = false): XColumn {\n    const names = this.names;\n    const start = this.firstCategory;\n    const length = names?.length;\n    let snapshot: readonly string[] | undefined;\n    return {\n      kind: this.kind, values,\n      get categories() {\n        return names === null || !snapshotCategories && start === 0 ? names : (snapshot ??= names.slice(start, length));\n      },\n      timeZone: this.timeZone, dateUnit: this.kind === 'date' ? this.dateUnit ?? 'day' : null,\n      ordered: this.kind === 'category' && this.field.ordered,\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nexport function dailyDelta(delta: number): number {\n  const days = Math.round(delta / DAY);\n  return days > 0 && Math.abs(delta - days * DAY) <= HOUR ? days * DAY : delta;\n}\n\nexport function sameDailyTime(first: number, position: number): boolean {\n  const delta = position - first;\n  return Math.abs(delta - Math.round(delta / DAY) * DAY) <= HOUR;\n}\n\nconst positionFormats = new Map<string, Intl.DateTimeFormat>();\n\nexport function positionName(axis: Pick<XColumn, 'kind' | 'dateUnit' | 'timeZone' | 'categories'>, position: number): string {\n  if (axis.kind === 'category') return JSON.stringify(axis.categories?.[position] ?? position);\n  if (axis.kind === 'number') return String(position);\n  if (axis.kind === 'time') {\n    const zone = axis.timeZone ?? 'UTC';\n    if (zone === 'UTC') return new Date(position).toISOString();\n    let format = positionFormats.get(zone);\n    if (!format) {\n      format = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-CA', {\n        timeZone: zone, year: 'numeric', month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit',\n        hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit', fractionalSecondDigits: 3, hourCycle: 'h23',\n      });\n      positionFormats.set(zone, format);\n    }\n    return format.format(position) + ' ' + zone;\n  }\n  const iso = new Date(position).toISOString();\n  if (axis.kind === 'wall') return iso.slice(0, -1);\n  return iso.slice(0, axis.dateUnit === 'year' ? -20 : axis.dateUnit === 'month' ? -17 : -14);\n}\nimport type { DiagnosticSink, ResolvedReference, XColumn, XKind } from '../core/contracts';\nimport type { ResolvedXField } from '../data';\nimport { Reports } from '../data/reports';\nimport { nameOf, XParser } from '../data/x';\nimport { report } from '../diagnostics';\nimport { diagnosticContext, type DiagnosticCode } from '../diagnostics/registry';\nimport type { Reference, XValue } from '../public';\n\nexport type Span<T = number> = readonly [T, T];\n\ninterface Option {\n  readonly field: string;\n  readonly sink: DiagnosticSink;\n  readonly axisPosition?: boolean;\n  readonly detail?: string;\n}\n\ntype PositionReader = (value: XValue, option?: Option) => number;\n\nexport function positionReader(\n  x: Pick<XColumn, 'kind' | 'categories' | 'timeZone'>,\n  field: ResolvedXField | undefined,\n): PositionReader {\n  if (x.kind === 'category') return (value, option) => {\n    const name = nameOf(value);\n    const index = name === null ? -1 : x.categories?.indexOf(name) ?? -1;\n    if (index >= 0) return index;\n    if (option) report(option.sink, 'AX107', 'none', {\n      field: option.field, detail: option.detail, outcome: 'The option is ignored.',\n    });\n    return NaN;\n  };\n  const resolved: ResolvedXField = field ?? {\n    field: 'x', label: 'x', unit: null, type: x.kind === 'wall' || x.kind === 'number' ? null : x.kind,\n    timeZone: x.timeZone ?? 'UTC', ordered: false, format: null, tickFormat: null, domain: null,\n  };\n  const parser = new XParser(resolved, x.kind, { timeZone: x.timeZone ?? 'UTC' });\n  return (value, option) => {\n    if (option?.axisPosition && x.kind !== 'number' && typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value)) return value;\n    const reports = new Reports(option?.field ?? resolved.field);\n    const position = parser.read(value, -1, reports);\n    // The parser's diagnostics still apply, but an option has no source row or omitted data values.\n    if (option) reports.flush({\n      add(diagnostic) {\n        const context = diagnosticContext(diagnostic);\n        report(option.sink, diagnostic.code as DiagnosticCode, 'none', {\n          ...context, field: diagnostic.field, count: diagnostic.count,\n          detail: diagnostic.effect === 'omitted' ? option.detail : context?.detail,\n          outcome: diagnostic.effect === 'omitted' ? 'The option is ignored.' : context?.outcome,\n        });\n      },\n    });\n    return position;\n  };\n}\n\nexport function readSpan(\n  input: Span<XValue> | null | undefined, read: PositionReader, field: string, sink: DiagnosticSink,\n  ordered = false,\n): Span | null {\n  if (!input) return null;\n  const option = { field, sink, axisPosition: true, detail: 'Supply two bounds in the x axis format.' };\n  const a = read(input[0], option);\n  const b = read(input[1], option);\n  if (!Number.isFinite(a) || !Number.isFinite(b) || ordered && a >= b) return null;\n  return [Math.min(a, b), Math.max(a, b)];\n}\n\nfunction isPair<T>(value: T | Span<T>): value is Span<T> {\n  return Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nexport function resolveReferences(\n  input: readonly Reference[], readX: PositionReader, xKind: XKind, sink: DiagnosticSink,\n): ResolvedReference[] {\n  const references: ResolvedReference[] = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < input.length; i++) {\n    const { x, y, label } = input[i]!;\n    const add = (axis: 'x' | 'y', from: number, to: number) => {\n      references.push({ axis, from: Math.min(from, to), to: Math.max(from, to), label });\n    };\n    if (x !== undefined) {\n      const pair = isPair(x);\n      const option = {\n        field: 'reference[' + i + '].x', sink,\n        detail: xKind === 'category' ? 'Use an existing category for each bound.' : 'Supply a reference in the x axis format.',\n      };\n      const from = readX(pair ? x[0] : x, option);\n      const to = pair ? readX(x[1], option) : from;\n      if (Number.isFinite(from) && Number.isFinite(to)) add('x', from, to);\n    }\n    if (y !== undefined) {\n      const pair = isPair(y);\n      const from = pair ? y[0] : y;\n      const to = pair ? y[1] : from;\n      if (Number.isFinite(from) && Number.isFinite(to)) {\n        add('y', from, to);\n      } else {\n        report(sink, 'AX103', 'none', { field: 'reference[' + i + '].y' });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return references;\n}\nimport type { XKind } from '../core/contracts';\nimport { normalize, resolveOptions } from '../data';\nimport type { XValue } from '../public';\n\nconst ignoreDiagnostics = { add() {} };\nconst version = { epoch: 0, revision: 0 };\n\nexport function readPosition(\n  value: XValue, kind: XKind, zone: string | null, categories: readonly string[] | null = null,\n): number {\n  if (kind === 'category') {\n    const i = value instanceof Date ? -1 : categories?.indexOf(String(value)) ?? -1;\n    if (i >= 0) return i;\n    return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isInteger(value) ? value : NaN;\n  }\n  if (typeof value === 'number') return value;\n\n  // Use the data entry point on a single row until it exports a standalone x parser.\n  const timeZone = zone ?? 'UTC';\n  const options = resolveOptions('line', {\n    data: [{ x: value, y: 0 }], x: { field: 'x', type: kind === 'wall' ? undefined : kind, timeZone }, y: 'y',\n  }, ignoreDiagnostics);\n  const frame = normalize('line', options, { timeZone }, ignoreDiagnostics, version);\n  return frame.shape === 'aligned' && frame.x.kind === kind ? frame.x.values[0] ?? NaN : NaN;\n}\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport fc from 'fast-check';\nimport { SLOT_GAP, SLOT_NULL, SLOT_VALUE } from '../../src/core/contracts';\nimport { AlignedStore } from '../../src/data';\nimport { DiagnosticCollector } from '../../src/diagnostics';\nimport { aligned, contents, utc, version } from './helpers';\n\nfunction store(options: unknown, sink?: DiagnosticCollector): AlignedStore {\n  return new AlignedStore('line', aligned(options).resolved, utc, version, sink);\n}\n\ndescribe('streaming', () => {\n  it('extends owned buffers with views and preserves older revisions', () => {\n    const data = [{ x: 0, y: 100 }, { x: 1, y: 101 }, { x: 2, y: 102 }];\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const before = stream.frame;\n    const appended = { x: 3, y: 103 };\n    const after = stream.append([appended]);\n    expect(after.x.values.buffer).toBe(before.x.values.buffer);\n    expect(after.series[0]!.y.buffer).toBe(before.series[0]!.y.buffer);\n    expect(after.series[0]!.slot.buffer).toBe(before.series[0]!.slot.buffer);\n    expect(after.series[0]!.row?.buffer).toBe(before.series[0]!.row?.buffer);\n    expect([...before.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1, 2]);\n    expect([...before.series[0]!.y]).toEqual([100, 101, 102]);\n    expect([...after.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, 3]);\n    expect([...after.series[0]!.y]).toEqual([100, 101, 102, 103]);\n    expect([...after.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, 3]);\n    expect(after.epoch).toBe(before.epoch);\n    expect(after.revision).toBe(before.revision + 1);\n    expect(before.source.rowAt(3)).toBeNull();\n    expect(after.source.rowAt(3)).toBe(appended);\n  });\n\n  it('streams from borrowed columns and uses the row meaning of NaN for appends', () => {\n    const data = { columns: { x: Float64Array.of(0, 1, 2), y: Float32Array.of(6, NaN, 8) } };\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const added = { x: 3, y: NaN };\n    const next = stream.append([added]);\n    expect([...next.series[0]!.y]).toEqual([6, NaN, 8, NaN]);\n    expect(next.series[0]!.slot[1]).toBe(SLOT_NULL);\n    expect(next.source.rowAt(1)).toEqual({ x: 1, y: NaN });\n    expect(next.source.rowAt(3)).toBe(added);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX103', rows: [3], count: 1 }]);\n    const earlier = { x: -1, y: 5 };\n    const fallback = stream.append([earlier]);\n    expect([...fallback.x.values]).toEqual([-1, 0, 1, 2, 3]);\n    expect([...fallback.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([4, 0, 1, 2, 3]);\n    expect(fallback.series[0]!.slot[2]).toBe(SLOT_NULL);\n    expect(fallback.source.rowAt(4)).toBe(earlier);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX103', rows: [3] }, { code: 'AX151', rows: [4] }]);\n    expect([...data.columns.y]).toEqual([6, NaN, 8]);\n  });\n\n  it('streams multiple wide fields and a growing long series set', () => {\n    const prior = [{ x: 1, a: 1, b: null }, { x: 2, a: 2, b: 20 }];\n    const wide = store({ data: prior, x: 'x', y: ['a', 'b'] });\n    const more = [{ x: 3, a: 3, b: 30 }];\n    const wideNext = wide.append(more);\n    expect(wideNext.series.map(s => [...s.y])).toEqual([[1, 2, 3], [NaN, 20, 30]]);\n    expect(contents(wideNext)).toEqual(contents(aligned({ data: [...prior, ...more], x: 'x', y: ['a', 'b'] }).frame));\n\n    const initial = [{ x: 1, y: 1, name: 'A' }];\n    const additions = [{ x: 1, y: 7, name: 'B' }, { x: 2, y: 2, name: 'A' }, { x: 3, y: 5, name: 'C' }];\n    const long = store({ data: initial, x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 'name' });\n    const before = long.frame;\n    for (const row of additions) long.append([row]);\n    expect(contents(long.frame)).toEqual(contents(aligned({\n      data: [...initial, ...additions], x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 'name',\n    }).frame));\n    expect(before.series).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect([...before.series[0]!.y]).toEqual([1]);\n    expect(long.diagnostics).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it('extends an established grid with a new gap without copying previous slots', () => {\n    const data = [0, 1, 2].map(x => ({ x, y: x }));\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const before = stream.frame;\n    const after = stream.append([{ x: 4, y: 4 }]);\n    expect(after.x.values.buffer).toBe(before.x.values.buffer);\n    expect([...after.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);\n    expect([...after.series[0]!.slot]).toEqual([SLOT_VALUE, SLOT_VALUE, SLOT_VALUE, SLOT_GAP, SLOT_VALUE]);\n    expect([...after.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, -1, 3]);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX105', count: 1 }]);\n  });\n\n  it('removes inferred gaps when more observations invalidate the old cadence', () => {\n    const data = [0, 1, 2, 4].map(x => ({ x, y: x }));\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const before = stream.frame;\n    const after = stream.append([{ x: 4.5, y: 10 }]);\n    expect([...before.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);\n    expect([...after.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1, 2, 4, 4.5]);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it('retains the latest observed positions along with interior gaps and evicts original source rows', () => {\n    const data = [0, 1, 2, 4].map(x => ({ x, y: x }));\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const newest = { x: 5, y: 5 };\n    const frame = stream.append([newest], { keep: 3 });\n    expect([...frame.x.values]).toEqual([2, 3, 4, 5]);\n    expect([...frame.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([2, -1, 3, 4]);\n    expect(frame.source.rowAt(0)).toBeNull();\n    expect(frame.source.rowAt(1)).toBeNull();\n    expect(frame.source.rowAt(2)).toBe(data[2]);\n    expect(frame.source.rowAt(4)).toBe(newest);\n    const older = { x: 1, y: 20 };\n    const outOfOrder = stream.append([older], { keep: 2 });\n    expect([...outOfOrder.x.values]).toEqual([4, 5]);\n    expect([...outOfOrder.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([3, 4]);\n    expect(outOfOrder.source.rowAt(5)).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it('evicts unused categories, rebases their indexes, and keeps old category views immutable', () => {\n    const data = [{ x: 'Monday', y: 1 }, { x: 'Tuesday', y: 2 }];\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const before = stream.frame;\n    const after = stream.append([{ x: 'Wednesday', y: 3 }], { keep: 2 });\n    expect(before.x.categories).toEqual(['Monday', 'Tuesday']);\n    expect(after.x.categories).toEqual(['Tuesday', 'Wednesday']);\n    expect([...after.x.values]).toEqual([0, 1]);\n    expect([...after.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([1, 2]);\n  });\n\n  it('leaves the frame and category state untouched if a diagnostic sink rejects an append', () => {\n    const stream = store({ data: [{ x: 'Mon', y: 1 }], x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const initial = stream.frame;\n    expect(() => stream.append([{ x: 'Tue', y: Infinity }], {}, {\n      add(diagnostic) { if (diagnostic.level === 'warning') throw new Error(diagnostic.code); },\n    })).toThrow('AX103');\n    expect(stream.frame).toBe(initial);\n    const next = stream.append([{ x: 'Wed', y: 3 }]);\n    expect(next.x.categories).toEqual(['Mon', 'Wed']);\n    expect([...next.series[0]!.row!]).toEqual([0, 1]);\n  });\n\n  it('revalidates earlier decimal strings when a later row makes the column mixed', () => {\n    const stream = store({ data: [{ x: 0, y: '1' }], x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    expect(stream.frame.series[0]!.y[0]).toBe(1);\n    const frame = stream.append([{ x: 1, y: 2 }]);\n    expect([...frame.series[0]!.y]).toEqual([NaN, 2]);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX106', rows: [0], count: 1 }]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('streaming invariants', () => {\n  const data = fc.array(fc.record({\n    x: fc.integer({ min: -24, max: 24 }),\n    y: fc.oneof(fc.integer(), fc.constant(null), fc.constant(undefined), fc.constant(NaN), fc.constant('5')),\n  }), { maxLength: 35 });\n\n  it('matches full normalization when adding the same rows one by one', () => {\n    fc.assert(fc.property(data, fc.boolean(), (rows, shuffle) => {\n      const input = shuffle ? rows : [...rows].sort((a, b) => a.x - b.x);\n      const options = { data: input, x: 'x', y: 'y' };\n      const stream = store({ ...options, data: [] });\n      for (const row of input) stream.append([row]);\n      const whole = aligned(options).frame;\n      expect(contents(stream.frame)).toEqual(contents(whole));\n    }), { numRuns: 150 });\n  });\n\n  it('never keeps more than k distinct observed positions and always keeps the latest ones', () => {\n    fc.assert(fc.property(data, fc.integer({ min: 0, max: 10 }), (rows, keep) => {\n      const stream = store({ data: [], x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n      const seen = new Set<number>();\n      for (const row of rows) {\n        const frame = stream.append([row], { keep });\n        seen.add(row.x);\n        const expected = keep === 0 ? [] : [...seen].sort((a, b) => a - b).slice(-keep);\n        const observed = [...frame.x.values].filter((_, i) => frame.series.some(series => series.row![i]! >= 0));\n        expect(observed).toEqual(expected);\n        expect(observed.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(keep);\n      }\n    }), { numRuns: 150 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('diagnostics in a retained window', () => {\n  it('discards diagnostics with their rows and lets a series draw after its duplicate x leaves', () => {\n    const data = [{ x: 0, y: 1 }, { x: 1, y: NaN }];\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    const first = stream.frame;\n    const duplicate = stream.append([{ x: 1, y: 9 }]);\n    expect(duplicate.x.values.buffer).toBe(first.x.values.buffer);\n    expect(duplicate.series[0]!.y.buffer).toBe(first.series[0]!.y.buffer);\n    expect(first.series[0]!.drawable).toBe(true);\n    expect(duplicate.series[0]!.drawable).toBe(false);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics.map(d => [d.code, d.rows])).toEqual([['AX103', [1]], ['AX108', [2]]]);\n    const latest = stream.append([{ x: 2, y: 2 }, { x: 3, y: 3 }], { keep: 2 });\n    expect(latest.series[0]!.drawable).toBe(true);\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toEqual([]);\n    expect(latest.source.rowAt(1)).toBeNull();\n    expect(latest.source.rowAt(2)).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it('retains only examples and counts within the active window after the original examples are evicted', () => {\n    const data = Array.from({ length: 15 }, (_, i) => ({ x: i, y: NaN }));\n    const stream = store({ data, x: 'x', y: 'y' });\n    stream.append([{ x: 15, y: NaN }], { keep: 4 });\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX103', count: 4, rows: [12, 13, 14, 15] }]);\n  });\n\n  it('recovers the daily-calendar hint when eviction removes a non-daily interval', () => {\n    const x = { field: 'x', type: 'time' };\n    const days = [Date.UTC(2026, 2, 7), Date.UTC(2026, 2, 8), Date.UTC(2026, 2, 9), Date.UTC(2026, 2, 10)];\n    const data = [{ x: days[0]! - 3600_000, y: 4 }, ...days.slice(0, 3).map(x => ({ x, y: 5 }))];\n    const stream = store({ data, x, y: 'y' });\n    expect(stream.diagnostics.map(d => d.code)).not.toContain('AX111');\n    stream.append([{ x: days[3], y: 6 }], { keep: 3 });\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toMatchObject([{ code: 'AX111', count: 3, rows: [2, 3, 4] }]);\n    stream.append([], { keep: 1 });\n    expect(stream.diagnostics).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\nit('matches full long-form normalization when series arrive one row at a time at shared x positions', () => {\n  fc.assert(fc.property(fc.array(fc.record({\n    x: fc.integer({ min: 0, max: 20 }),\n    y: fc.oneof(fc.integer(), fc.constant(null)),\n    series: fc.constantFrom('a', 'b', 'c'),\n  }), { maxLength: 40 }), rows => {\n    const data = [...rows].sort((a, b) => a.x - b.x);\n    const options = { data, x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 'series' };\n    const stream = store({ ...options, data: [] });\n    for (const row of data) stream.append([row]);\n    expect(contents(stream.frame)).toEqual(contents(aligned(options).frame));\n  }));\n});\n\nit('matches full normalization across batches, retained windows and older revisions', () => {\n  const samples = fc.array(fc.record({\n    advance: fc.integer({ min: 1, max: 3 }),\n    groups: fc.subarray(['a', 'b', 'c'], { minLength: 1 }),\n    y: fc.oneof(fc.integer(), fc.constant(null)),\n  }), { minLength: 1, maxLength: 30 });\n  const shapes = fc.constantFrom('number', 'date', 'month', 'time', 'wall', 'category');\n  type SampleRow = { x: number | string; y: number | null } &\n    ({ s: string } | { a: number | null; b: number | null; c: number | null });\n  fc.assert(fc.property(samples, shapes, fc.boolean(), fc.array(fc.integer({ min: 1, max: 5 }), { minLength: 1, maxLength: 8 }),\n    fc.option(fc.integer({ min: 1, max: 8 }), { nil: undefined }), (samples, kind, long, sizes, keep) => {\n      const values = ['a', 'b', 'c'];\n      const encoding = long ? { x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's' } : { x: 'x', y: values };\n      const makeX = (n: number): number | string => {\n        if (kind === 'number') return n / 10;\n        if (kind === 'category') return 'item ' + n;\n        if (kind === 'month') return new Date(Date.UTC(2026, n, 1)).toISOString().slice(0, 7);\n        const iso = new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 2, 1 + n)).toISOString();\n        if (kind === 'date') return iso.slice(0, 10);\n        if (kind === 'wall') return iso.replace('T', ' ').slice(0, -1);\n        return iso;\n      };\n      let n = 0;\n      const data = samples.flatMap<SampleRow>(({ advance, groups, y }) => {\n        n += advance;\n        const x = makeX(n);\n        return long ? groups.map(s => ({ x, y, s })) : [{ x, y, a: y, b: y, c: y }];\n      });\n      const streaming = store({ data: [], ...encoding });\n      const revisions: { frame: typeof streaming.frame; snapshot: ReturnType<typeof contents> }[] = [];\n      for (let start = 0, batch = 0; start < data.length; batch++) {\n        const end = Math.min(data.length, start + sizes[batch % sizes.length]!);\n        const frame = streaming.append(data.slice(start, end), { keep });\n        const snapshot = contents(frame);\n        revisions.push({ frame, snapshot });\n        const observed = [...new Set(data.slice(0, end).map(row => row.x))];\n        const window = new Set(keep === undefined ? observed : observed.slice(-keep));\n        const kept = data.slice(0, end).map((row, i) => ({ row, i })).filter(({ row }) => window.has(row.x));\n        const full = contents(aligned({ data: kept.map(({ row }) => row), ...encoding }).frame);\n        const remapped = full.series.map(series => ({ ...series, row: series.row.map(row => row < 0 ? row : kept[row]!.i) }));\n        const byKey = (a: { key: string }, b: { key: string }) => a.key.localeCompare(b.key);\n        expect({ ...snapshot, series: [...snapshot.series].sort(byKey) }).toEqual({ ...full, series: remapped.sort(byKey) });\n        start = end;\n      }\n      for (const { frame, snapshot } of revisions) expect(contents(frame)).toEqual(snapshot);\n    }), { numRuns: 150 });\n});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
